-sub-neighborhood total_included_n_reps The minimum valid value is 0_int32 . integer(kind=int32), intent(in) :: k_families Number of sub-neighborhoods analyzed real(kind=real64), intent(out), dimension(k_families) :: support_weights Per-sub-neighborhood calculated support weight (ratio between its total_included_n_reps and sum(total_included_n_reps_per_f) , zero if there were no replicates included at all) real(kind=real64), intent(out), dimension(k_families) :: contribution_scores Per-sub-neighborhood calculated contribution ( ) integer(kind=int32), intent(out) :: ierr Error code; zero on success, non-zero on failure.","tags":"","url":"module/tox_data_integration_per_family.html"},{"title":"f42_binary_search_tree – TensorOmics","text":"Flat-index-based Binary Search Tree (BST) utilities for 1D range queries.\nThis module provides routines to build a BST index (via sorting), access sorted values,\nand perform range queries over a real-valued array using the sorted index. Generated from f42_binary_search_tree_impl ; do not edit -- regenerate instead. Uses iso_fortran_env f42_binary_search_tree_impl tox_errors f42_sort_impl Subroutines public pure subroutine build_bst_index (values, n_values, sorted_indices, ierr) Validates its inputs, then calls build_bst_index_impl . Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=real64), intent(in), dimension(n_values) :: values Input real array to be indexed integer(kind=int32), intent(in) :: n_values Number of elements in values array integer(kind=int32), intent(out), dimension(n_values) :: sorted_indices Output permutation index integer(kind=int32), intent(out) :: ierr Error code; zero on success, non-zero on failure. public pure subroutine bst_range_query (values, n_values, lower_bound, upper_bound, output_indices, n_matches, ierr) Validates its inputs, prepares what bst_range_query_impl needs, then calls it. The entry point to reach for first; see bst_range_query_expert to prepare it yourself. Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=real64), intent(in), dimension(n_values) :: values Input real array integer(kind=int32), intent(in) :: n_values Number of elements real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: lower_bound Lower bound of range (inclusive)\nThe maximum valid value is upper_bound . real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: upper_bound Upper bound of range (inclusive) integer(kind=int32), intent(out), dimension(n_values) :: output_indices Output array of matching indices.\nThe first n_matches elements will hold the results. integer(kind=int32), intent(out) :: n_matches Number of matches found integer(kind=int32), intent(out) :: ierr Error code; zero on success, non-zero on failure. public pure subroutine bst_range_query_expert (values, values_perm, n_values, lower_bound, upper_bound, output_indices, n_matches, ierr) Validates its inputs, then calls bst_range_query_impl with what you supply. The expert entry point: it allocates nothing and prepares nothing; bst_range_query does both. Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=real64), intent(in), dimension(n_values) :: values Input real array integer(kind=int32), intent(in), dimension(n_values) :: values_perm Permutation of values in ascending order -- the BST index. The allocating entry\npoint builds and heapsorts it for you; the expert one takes whatever order you\nsupply, so a caller that already holds one from build_bst_index can reuse it across queries.\nThe minimum valid value is 1_int32 .\nThe maximum valid value is n_values . integer(kind=int32), intent(in) :: n_values Number of elements real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: lower_bound Lower bound of range (inclusive)\nThe maximum valid value is upper_bound . real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: upper_bound Upper bound of range (inclusive) integer(kind=int32), intent(out), dimension(n_values) :: output_indices Output array of matching indices.\nThe first n_matches elements will hold the results. integer(kind=int32), intent(out) :: n_matches Number of matches found integer(kind=int32), intent(out) :: ierr Error code; zero on success, non-zero on failure.","tags":"","url":"module/f42_binary_search_tree.html"},{"title":"tox_normalization_impl – TensorOmics","text":"Normalization of expression data: putting samples on a comparable scale before anything\ndistance-based is computed from them. Several schemes, each its own entry point rather than a mode: a log2 transformation, scaling\nby standard deviation (LOESS-smoothed against expression level, so the correction follows the\nmean-variance trend rather than assuming one), root-mean-square scaling, quantile\nnormalization, and normalization to unit length. normalization_pipeline chains them in the order the analysis expects, and is what most\ncallers want. The individual routines are published for a caller assembling their own. Uses iso_fortran_env iso_c_binding f42_math_impl f42_vector_impl f42_safeguard tox_errors tox_loess_impl Subroutines public pure subroutine normalize_unit_length_impl (vector, n_dims, ierr) Author Franz-Eric Sill License MIT Normalizes an input vector to unit length in-place Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=real64), intent(inout), dimension(n_dims) :: vector Vector that will be normalized to unit length\nNaN is permitted for this value.\nInfinite values are permitted for this value. integer(kind=int32), intent(in) :: n_dims number of elements in vector integer(kind=int32), intent(out) :: ierr Error code public  subroutine normalization_pipeline_impl (n_genes, n_replicates, expr, log_transformed_expr, reps_per_tissue, n_tissues, tmp_expr_copy, tmp_loess_y, tmp_indices_used, tmp_yhat_global, tmp_int_workspace, int_workspace_size, tmp_real_workspace, real_workspace_size, tmp_hat_diag, tmp_loess_weights, tmp_eval_points, tmp_robust_weights, tmp_combined_weights, tmp_residuals, tmp_permutation_indices, span, degree, use_quantile, ierr) Author Vivian Bass License MIT Complete normalization pipeline for gene expression data. Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer(kind=int32), intent(in) :: n_genes Number of genes (rows) integer(kind=int32), intent(in) :: n_replicates Number of replicates per gene real(kind=real64), intent(in), dimension(n_replicates, n_genes) :: expr Gene Expression matrix\nNaN is permitted for this value.\nInfinite values are permitted for this value. real(kind=real64), intent(out), dimension(n_tissues, n_genes), target :: log_transformed_expr Log-transformed grouped expr integer(kind=int32), intent(in), dimension(n_tissues) :: reps_per_tissue Number of replicates per tissue in expr . It describes, which slices in expr relate to which tissue,\ne.g. [2,3] means 5 total replicates per gene, the first two of which belong to the first tissue and the remaining three to the second. integer(kind=int32), intent(in) :: n_tissues Number of tissues real(kind=real64), intent(out), dimension(n_replicates, n_genes) :: tmp_expr_copy Work matrix the pipeline normalizes in place real(kind=real64), intent(out), dimension(n_genes), target :: tmp_loess_y Work vector for the empirical standard deviations (Y-axis for LOESS) integer(kind=int32), intent(out), dimension(n_genes) :: tmp_indices_used Work vector mapping the fitted points back to gene indices real(kind=real64), intent(out), dimension(n_genes), target :: tmp_yhat_global Work vector for the fitted standard deviations (LOESS predictions) integer(kind=int32), intent(out), dimension(int_workspace_size) :: tmp_int_workspace Integer workspace array integer(kind=int32), intent(in) :: int_workspace_size Length of integer workspace.\nIt is VERY IMPORTANT to compute this argument from the int_workspace_size output produced by tox_loess_required_workspace . Read more… real(kind=real64), intent(out), dimension(real_workspace_size) :: tmp_real_workspace Real workspace array integer(kind=int32), intent(in) :: real_workspace_size Length of real workspace.\nIt is VERY IMPORTANT to compute this argument from the real_workspace_size output produced by tox_loess_required_workspace . Read more… real(kind=real64), intent(out), dimension(n_genes) :: tmp_hat_diag Diagonal elements of the LOESS hat matrix real(kind=real64), intent(out), dimension(n_genes) :: tmp_loess_weights Per-point weights handed to the LOESS fit real(kind=real64), intent(out), dimension(n_genes, 1) :: tmp_eval_points Points the fitted curve is evaluated at real(kind=real64), intent(out), dimension(n_genes) :: tmp_robust_weights Robust bisquare weights of the LOESS fit real(kind=real64), intent(out), dimension(n_genes) :: tmp_combined_weights Combined weights of the LOESS fit real(kind=real64), intent(out), dimension(n_genes) :: tmp_residuals Residuals of the LOESS fit integer(kind=int32), intent(out), dimension(n_genes) :: tmp_permutation_indices Permutation indices of the LOESS fit real(kind=real64), intent(in), optional :: span LOESS span parameter.\nThe default value is 0.7_real64 . integer(kind=int32), intent(in), optional :: degree LOESS degree parameter.\nThe default value is 2_int32 . logical(kind=c_bool), intent(in), optional :: use_quantile Use quantile normalization.\nThe default value is .false. . integer(kind=int32), intent(out) :: ierr Error code public  subroutine normalize_by_std_dev_impl (n_genes, n_replicates, expr, normalized_expr, tmp_loess_x, tmp_loess_y, tmp_indices_used, tmp_yhat_global, tmp_int_workspace, int_workspace_size, tmp_real_workspace, real_workspace_size, tmp_hat_diag, tmp_loess_weights, tmp_eval_points, tmp_robust_weights, tmp_combined_weights, tmp_residuals, tmp_permutation_indices, span, degree, ierr) Author Vivian Bass License MIT Normalizes each gene's expression vector using LOESS-stabilized standard deviation. Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer(kind=int32), intent(in) :: n_genes Number of genes (rows) integer(kind=int32), intent(in) :: n_replicates Number of replicates per gene real(kind=real64), intent(in), dimension(n_replicates, n_genes) :: expr Gene Expression matrix\nNaN is permitted for this value.\nInfinite values are permitted for this value. real(kind=real64), intent(out), dimension(n_replicates, n_genes) :: normalized_expr Normalized expr real(kind=real64), intent(out), dimension(n_genes) :: tmp_loess_x Work vector for the mean values (X-axis for LOESS) real(kind=real64), intent(out), dimension(n_genes) :: tmp_loess_y Work vector for the empirical standard deviations (Y-axis for LOESS) integer(kind=int32), intent(out), dimension(n_genes) :: tmp_indices_used Work vector mapping the fitted points back to gene indices real(kind=real64), intent(out), dimension(n_genes) :: tmp_yhat_global Work vector for the fitted standard deviations (LOESS predictions) integer(kind=int32), intent(out), dimension(int_workspace_size) :: tmp_int_workspace Integer workspace array integer(kind=int32), intent(in) :: int_workspace_size Length of integer workspace.\nIt is VERY IMPORTANT to compute this argument from the int_workspace_size output produced by tox_loess_required_workspace . Read more… real(kind=real64), intent(out), dimension(real_workspace_size) :: tmp_real_workspace Real workspace array integer(kind=int32), intent(in) :: real_workspace_size Length of real workspace.\nIt is VERY IMPORTANT to compute this argument from the real_workspace_size output produced by tox_loess_required_workspace . Read more… real(kind=real64), intent(out), dimension(n_genes) :: tmp_hat_diag Diagonal elements of the LOESS hat matrix real(kind=real64), intent(out), dimension(n_genes) :: tmp_loess_weights Per-point weights handed to the LOESS fit real(kind=real64), intent(out), dimension(n_genes, 1) :: tmp_eval_points Points the fitted curve is evaluated at real(kind=real64), intent(out), dimension(n_genes) :: tmp_robust_weights Robust bisquare weights of the LOESS fit real(kind=real64), intent(out), dimension(n_genes) :: tmp_combined_weights Combined weights of the LOESS fit real(kind=real64), intent(out), dimension(n_genes) :: tmp_residuals Residuals of the LOESS fit integer(kind=int32), intent(out), dimension(n_genes) :: tmp_permutation_indices Permutation indices of the LOESS fit real(kind=real64), intent(in), optional :: span LOESS span parameter.\nThe default value is 0.7_real64 . integer(kind=int32), intent(in), optional :: degree LOESS degree parameter.\nThe default value is 2_int32 . integer(kind=int32), intent(out) :: ierr Error code public  subroutine normalize_by_std_dev_inplace_helper (n_genes, n_replicates, expr, tmp_loess_x, tmp_loess_y, tmp_indices_used, tmp_yhat_global, tmp_int_workspace, int_workspace_size, tmp_real_workspace, real_workspace_size, tmp_hat_diag, tmp_loess_weights, tmp_eval_points, tmp_robust_weights, tmp_combined_weights, tmp_residuals, tmp_permutation_indices, span, degree, ierr) Author Vivian Bass License MIT Normalizes each gene's expression vector using LOESS-stabilized standard deviation.\nThis procedure applies a global stabilization based on the relationship between\ngene-wise mean expression and empirical standard deviation. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer(kind=int32), intent(in) :: n_genes Number of genes (rows) integer(kind=int32), intent(in) :: n_replicates Number of replicates per gene real(kind=real64), intent(inout), dimension(n_replicates, n_genes) :: expr Gene Expression matrix real(kind=real64), intent(out), dimension(n_genes) :: tmp_loess_x Mean values (X-axis for LOESS) real(kind=real64), intent(out), dimension(n_genes) :: tmp_loess_y Empirical standard deviation values (Y-axis for LOESS) integer(kind=int32), intent(out), dimension(n_genes) :: tmp_indices_used Mapping back to gene indices real(kind=real64), intent(out), dimension(n_genes) :: tmp_yhat_global Fitted standard deviation values (LOESS predictions) integer(kind=int32), intent(out), dimension(int_workspace_size) :: tmp_int_workspace Integer workspace array integer(kind=int32), intent(in) :: int_workspace_size Length of integer workspace real(kind=real64), intent(out), dimension(real_workspace_size) :: tmp_real_workspace Real workspace array integer(kind=int32), intent(in) :: real_workspace_size Length of real workspace real(kind=real64), intent(out), dimension(n_genes) :: tmp_hat_diag Diagonal elements of the LOESS hat matrix real(kind=real64), intent(out), dimension(n_genes) :: tmp_loess_weights Per-point weights handed to the LOESS fit real(kind=real64), intent(out), dimension(n_genes, 1) :: tmp_eval_points Points the fitted curve is evaluated at real(kind=real64), intent(out), dimension(n_genes) :: tmp_robust_weights Robust bisquare weights of the LOESS fit real(kind=real64), intent(out), dimension(n_genes) :: tmp_combined_weights Combined weights of the LOESS fit real(kind=real64), intent(out), dimension(n_genes) :: tmp_residuals Residuals of the LOESS fit integer(kind=int32), intent(out), dimension(n_genes) :: tmp_permutation_indices Permutation indices of the LOESS fit real(kind=real64), intent(in), optional :: span LOESS span parameter.\nThe default value is 0.7_real64 . integer(kind=int32), intent(in), optional :: degree LOESS degree parameter.\nThe default value is 2_int32 . integer(kind=int32), intent(out) :: ierr Error code public pure subroutine root_mean_sq_normalization_impl (n_genes, n_replicates, expr, normalized_expr) Author Vivian Bass License MIT Normalizes each gene's expression vector using sqrt(mean(x&#94;2)) Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer(kind=int32), intent(in) :: n_genes Number of genes (rows) integer(kind=int32), intent(in) :: n_replicates Number of replicates per gene real(kind=real64), intent(in), dimension(n_replicates, n_genes) :: expr Gene Expression matrix\nNaN is permitted for this value.\nInfinite values are permitted for this value. real(kind=real64), intent(out), dimension(n_replicates, n_genes) :: normalized_expr Normalized expr public pure subroutine root_mean_sq_normalization_inplace_helper (n_genes, n_replicates, expr) Author Vivian Bass License MIT Normalizes each gene's expression vector using sqrt(mean(x&#94;2)) across tissues (not classical standard deviation). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer(kind=int32), intent(in) :: n_genes Number of genes (rows) integer(kind=int32), intent(in) :: n_replicates Number of replicates per gene real(kind=real64), intent(inout), dimension(n_replicates, n_genes) :: expr Gene Expression matrix public pure subroutine quantile_normalization_impl (n_genes, n_replicates, expr, normalized_expr, rank_means, tmp_genes_row, tmp_perm) Author Vivian Bass License MIT Quantile normalization of a gene expression matrix (F42-compliant). Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer(kind=int32), intent(in) :: n_genes Number of genes (rows) integer(kind=int32), intent(in) :: n_replicates Number of replicates per gene real(kind=real64), intent(in), dimension(n_replicates, n_genes) :: expr Gene Expression matrix\nNaN is permitted for this value.\nInfinite values are permitted for this value. real(kind=real64), intent(out), dimension(n_replicates, n_genes) :: normalized_expr Normalized expr real(kind=real64), intent(out), dimension(n_genes) :: rank_means The mean of each rank across tissues, one per gene real(kind=real64), intent(out), dimension(n_genes) :: tmp_genes_row Temporary vector for sorting a tissue in expr across genes integer(kind=int32), intent(out), dimension(n_genes) :: tmp_perm Permutation vector public pure subroutine quantile_normalization_inplace_helper (n_genes, n_replicates, expr, rank_means, tmp_genes_row, tmp_perm) Author Vivian Bass License MIT Quantile normalization of a gene expression matrix (F42-compliant).\nComputes average expression per rank across tissues. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer(kind=int32), intent(in) :: n_genes Number of genes (rows) integer(kind=int32), intent(in) :: n_replicates Number of replicates per gene real(kind=real64), intent(inout), dimension(n_replicates, n_genes) :: expr Gene Expression matrix real(kind=real64), intent(out), dimension(n_genes) :: rank_means The mean of each rank across tissues, one per gene real(kind=real64), intent(out), dimension(n_genes) :: tmp_genes_row Temporary vector for sorting a tissue in expr across genes integer(kind=int32), intent(out), dimension(n_genes) :: tmp_perm Permutation vector public pure subroutine log2_transformation_impl (n_genes, n_tissues, expr, transformed_expr, ierr) Author Vivian Bass License MIT Apply log2(x + 1) transformation to each element of the input matrix. Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer(kind=int32), intent(in) :: n_genes Number of genes (rows) integer(kind=int32), intent(in) :: n_tissues Number of tissues real(kind=real64), intent(in), dimension(n_tissues, n_genes) :: expr Gene Expression matrix, from calc_tiss_avg NaN is permitted for this value.\nInfinite values are permitted for this value. real(kind=real64), intent(out), dimension(n_tissues, n_genes) :: transformed_expr Log-transformed expr integer(kind=int32), intent(out) :: ierr Error code public pure subroutine log2_transformation_inplace_helper (n_genes, n_tissues, expr, ierr) Author Vivian Bass License MIT Apply log2(x + 1) transformation to each element of the input matrix.\nThis subroutine performs element-wise log2(x + 1) transformation on a\nmatrix flattened in column-major order. The log2 is computed via: log(x + 1) / log(2) , which is numerically equivalent and avoids the\nnon-portable log2 intrinsic for compatibility with WebAssembly (WASM). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer(kind=int32), intent(in) :: n_genes Number of genes (rows) integer(kind=int32), intent(in) :: n_tissues Number of tissues real(kind=real64), intent(inout), dimension(n_tissues, n_genes) :: expr Gene Expression matrix, from calc_tiss_avg integer(kind=int32), intent(out) :: ierr Error code public pure subroutine calc_tiss_avg_impl (n_genes, n_tissues, reps_per_tissue, expr, tissue_averages) Author Vivian Bass License MIT Calculate tissue averages by averaging replicates within each tissue. Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer(kind=int32), intent(in) :: n_genes Number of genes (rows) integer(kind=int32), intent(in) :: n_tissues Number of tissues integer(kind=int32), intent(in), dimension(n_tissues) :: reps_per_tissue Number of replicates per tissue in expr . It describes, which slices in expr relate to which tissue,\ne.g. [2,3] means 5 total replicates per gene, the first two of which belong to the first tissue and the remaining three to the second.\nThe minimum valid value is 1_int32 . real(kind=real64), intent(in), dimension(sum(reps_per_tissue), n_genes) :: expr Gene Expression matrix\nNaN is permitted for this value.\nInfinite values are permitted for this value. real(kind=real64), intent(out), dimension(n_tissues, n_genes) :: tissue_averages Tissue averages per gene public pure subroutine calc_tiss_avg_helper (n_genes, n_tissues, reps_per_tissue, expr, tissue_averages) Author Vivian Bass License MIT (no input validation) Calculate tissue averages by averaging replicates within each group.\nFor each group of tissue replicates, this subroutine computes the average\nexpression per gene. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer(kind=int32), intent(in) :: n_genes Number of genes (rows) integer(kind=int32), intent(in) :: n_tissues Number of tissues integer(kind=int32), intent(in), dimension(n_tissues) :: reps_per_tissue Number of replicates per tissue in expr . It describes, which slices in expr relate to which tissue,\ne.g. [2,3] means 5 total replicates per gene, the first two of which belong to the first tissue and the remaining three to the second. real(kind=real64), intent(in), dimension(sum(reps_per_tissue), n_genes) :: expr Gene Expression matrix real(kind=real64), intent(out), dimension(n_tissues, n_genes) :: tissue_averages Tissue averages per gene public pure subroutine calc_fchange_impl (n_genes, n_tissues, n_pairs, control_tissues, condition_tissues, expr, fold_changes) Author Vivian Bass License MIT Calculate log2 fold changes between condition and control groups. Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer(kind=int32), intent(in) :: n_genes Number of genes (rows) integer(kind=int32), intent(in) :: n_tissues Number of tissues integer(kind=int32), intent(in) :: n_pairs Number of control-condition pairs integer(kind=int32), intent(in), dimension(n_pairs) :: control_tissues Control tissue indices\nThe minimum valid value is 1_int32 .\nThe maximum valid value is n_tissues . integer(kind=int32), intent(in), dimension(n_pairs) :: condition_tissues Condition tissue indices\nThe minimum valid value is 1_int32 .\nThe maximum valid value is n_tissues . real(kind=real64), intent(in), dimension(n_tissues, n_genes) :: expr Gene Expression matrix, from calc_tiss_avg NaN is permitted for this value.\nInfinite values are permitted for this value. real(kind=real64), intent(out), dimension(n_pairs, n_genes) :: fold_changes Output matrix for fold changes","tags":"","url":"module/tox_normalization_impl.html"},{"title":"f42_serde_arrays_utils_c – TensorOmics","text":"Module for array utilities. Defines the shared on-disk binary layout used by all typed array\nserialize/deserialize modules (int/real/complex/logical/char) and the\nheader read/write/validate helpers that implement it. The file header is\na fixed sequence of unformatted stream records, written and read in this\norder: magic number ( ARRAY_FILE_MAGIC ),\ntype code, number of dimensions ndim , then ndim dimension sizes. The\nraw array payload follows immediately after the header, written as one\ncontiguous block by the type-specific serializers. The header does NOT record the width of an element, so the payload is only\nreadable by a build that agrees with the writer on the storage size of the\ntype code. Logical arrays changed width once: they are now written as logical(c_bool) , one byte per element, where earlier builds wrote the\ndefault logical kind at four. A logical .bin file written before that\nchange therefore decodes to garbage here rather than failing, and one\nwritten here does the same there. No other type code has moved. Uses f42_safeguard iso_c_binding tox_errors Subroutines public  subroutine get_array_metadata_c (filename, filename_strlen, dims_out, dims_out_capacity, ndims, type_code, ierr) bind(C, name=\"get_array_metadata_c\") C-wrapper for get_array_metadata Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name character(kind=c_char, len=1), intent(in), dimension(filename_strlen), target :: filename Name of the file integer(kind=c_int), intent(in), target :: filename_strlen length of the strings in filename integer(kind=c_int), intent(out), dimension(dims_out_capacity), target :: dims_out Array to store output dimensions\nThe first ndims elements will hold the results. integer(kind=c_int), intent(in), target :: dims_out_capacity Capacity of the dims_out array integer(kind=c_int), intent(out), target :: ndims number of dimensions integer(kind=c_int), intent(out), target :: type_code Type code of the serialized array Read more… integer(kind=c_int), intent(out), target :: ierr Error code","tags":"","url":"module/f42_serde_arrays_utils_c.html"},{"title":"tox_loess_impl – TensorOmics","text":"LOESS local polynomial regression smoothing, over the netlib dloess / lowesd family. Two fits: loess_fit_plain and loess_fit_robust , the latter reweighting against outliers over\na number of iterations. There is deliberately no combined entry point dispatching on a mode --\na caller chooses the routine, and supplies the weights and the evaluation points it wants. A sample too degenerate to fit (fewer distinct points than the degree needs) is answered\ndirectly from the observations rather than handed to netlib, which cannot fit one and dies\ninside its decomposition instead of reporting. Nothing about that is visible to a caller\nbeyond the result. tox_loess_required_workspace sizes the workspace for a caller that wants to own it; the\nmode and iteration constants and EPS_LOESS are here for the same reason. The netlib\nroutines themselves are not re-documented beyond their calling convention. Uses iso_fortran_env iso_c_binding f42_math_impl f42_safeguard tox_errors Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial real(kind=real64), public, parameter :: EPS_LOESS = 1.0e-12_real64 Minimum allowed LOESS span and a general-purpose small epsilon used across this module\n(and by callers such as compute_family_scaling ) to\nguard against division/log by (near-)zero. Interfaces public        interface loess_decomposition public  subroutine lowesd(iv19_code, int_workspace, int_workspace_size, real_workspace_size, real_workspace, n_dim, n, span, degree, max_neighborhood_size, save_factorization) Perform LOESS decomposition.\nThis subroutine computes the decomposition of the LOESS model.\nIt initializes the integer and real workspace arrays based on the input parameters. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer(kind=int32), intent(in) :: iv19_code Packed netlib iv(19) model-selection code (family/surface/statistics digits); see loess_fit_plain for the fixed value used by this codebase. integer(kind=int32), intent(out) :: int_workspace (int_workspace_size) Integer workspace array, laid out and populated here; nothing in it is read integer(kind=int32), intent(in) :: int_workspace_size Length of the integer workspace array integer(kind=int32), intent(in) :: real_workspace_size Length of the real workspace array real(kind=real64), intent(out) :: real_workspace (real_workspace_size) Real workspace array, whose first entries are set here; nothing in it is read integer(kind=int32), intent(in) :: n_dim Dimensionality of the data integer(kind=int32), intent(in) :: n Number of data points real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: span Smoothing parameter for LOESS integer(kind=int32), intent(in) :: degree Degree of the LOESS polynomial integer(kind=int32), intent(in) :: max_neighborhood_size Maximum neighborhood size logical, intent(in) :: save_factorization Save matrix factorization flag public        interface loess_fitting public  subroutine lowesb(x, y, weights, hat_diag, compute_influence, int_workspace, int_workspace_size, real_workspace_size, real_workspace) Perform LOESS fitting.\nThis subroutine fits the LOESS model to the data.\nIt uses the input predictor and response variables to compute the diagonal elements of the hat matrix. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: x (*) Predictor variable array real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: y (*) Response variable array real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: weights (*) Weight array for data points real(kind=real64), intent(out) :: hat_diag (*) Diagonal elements of the hat matrix logical, intent(in) :: compute_influence Influence calculation flag integer(kind=int32), intent(inout) :: int_workspace (int_workspace_size) Integer workspace array integer(kind=int32), intent(in) :: int_workspace_size Length of the integer workspace array integer(kind=int32), intent(in) :: real_workspace_size Length of the real workspace array real(kind=real64), intent(inout) :: real_workspace (real_workspace_size) Real workspace array public        interface loess_evaluation public  subroutine lowese(int_workspace, int_workspace_size, real_workspace_size, real_workspace, n, eval_points, fitted_values) Perform LOESS evaluation.\nThis subroutine evaluates the LOESS model.\nIt computes the smoothed response variable array based on the input predictor variables. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer(kind=int32), intent(in) :: int_workspace (int_workspace_size) Integer workspace array, read as laid out by the decomposition and the fit integer(kind=int32), intent(in) :: int_workspace_size Length of the integer workspace array integer(kind=int32), intent(in) :: real_workspace_size Length of the real workspace array real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: real_workspace (real_workspace_size) Real workspace array, read as left by the fit integer(kind=int32), intent(in) :: n Number of data points real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: eval_points (n,1) x-values at which to evaluate the fitted LOESS curve (evaluation points) real(kind=real64), intent(out) :: fitted_values (n) Smoothed response variable array public        interface loess_robust_weights public  subroutine lowesw(residuals, n, robust_weights, permutation_indices) Compute robust weights for LOESS.\nThis subroutine computes the robust weights for the LOESS model.\nIt uses the residuals to update the weights for robust fitting. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: residuals (n) Residuals array integer(kind=int32), intent(in) :: n Number of data points real(kind=real64), intent(out) :: robust_weights (n) Robust weights array integer(kind=int32), intent(out) :: permutation_indices (n) Permutation indices array Subroutines public pure subroutine loess_degenerate_fit (n, x, y, degree, fitted_values, handled, ierr) Author Franz-Eric Sill License MIT Decides whether the data is too degenerate to fit, and answers it directly if so Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer(kind=int32), intent(in) :: n Total number of data points real(kind=real64), intent(in), dimension(n) :: x Predictor variable array real(kind=real64), intent(in), dimension(n) :: y Response variable array integer(kind=int32), intent(in) :: degree Degree of the LOESS polynomial real(kind=real64), intent(out), dimension(n) :: fitted_values Fitted values, written only when the fit was answered here logical(kind=c_bool), intent(out) :: handled .true. when the data was degenerate and fitted_values already holds the answer integer(kind=int32), intent(out) :: ierr Error code public  subroutine tox_loess_required_workspace (n_dim, max_neighborhood_size, int_workspace_size, real_workspace_size, save_factorization) Author Vivian Bass License MIT Category C-binding Recommend workspace sizes based on Netlib exact formulas Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer(kind=int32), intent(in) :: n_dim Dimensionality of the data integer(kind=int32), intent(in) :: max_neighborhood_size Maximum neighborhood size integer(kind=int32), intent(out) :: int_workspace_size Required size of the integer workspace array integer(kind=int32), intent(out) :: real_workspace_size Required size of the real workspace array logical(kind=c_bool), intent(in) :: save_factorization Save matrix factorization flag public  subroutine loess_fit_plain_impl (n, x, y, weights, eval_points, span, degree, max_neighborhood_size, compute_influence, save_factorization, tmp_int_workspace, int_workspace_size, tmp_real_workspace, real_workspace_size, tmp_hat_diag, fitted_values, ierr) Author Vivian Bass License MIT Perform plain LOESS fitting Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer(kind=int32), intent(in) :: n Total number of data points real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: x (n) Predictor variable array real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: y (n) Response variable array real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: weights (n) Weight array for data points real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: eval_points (n,1) Evaluation points (x values at which the fitted curve is computed) real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: span Smoothing parameter for LOESS\nThe minimum valid value is EPS_LOESS .\nThe maximum valid value is 1.0_real64 . integer(kind=int32), intent(in) :: degree Degree of the LOESS polynomial\nThe minimum valid value is 0_int32 .\nThe maximum valid value is 2_int32 . integer(kind=int32), intent(in) :: max_neighborhood_size Maximum neighborhood size logical(kind=c_bool), intent(in), optional :: compute_influence Influence calculation flag\nThe default value is .false. . logical(kind=c_bool), intent(in), optional :: save_factorization Save matrix factorization flag\nThe default value is .false. . integer(kind=int32), intent(out) :: tmp_int_workspace (int_workspace_size) Integer workspace array integer(kind=int32), intent(in) :: int_workspace_size Required size of the integer workspace array\nIt is VERY IMPORTANT to compute this argument from the int_workspace_size output produced by tox_loess_required_workspace .\nThe minimum valid value is 10000_int32 . Read more… real(kind=real64), intent(out) :: tmp_real_workspace (real_workspace_size) Real workspace array integer(kind=int32), intent(in) :: real_workspace_size Required size of the real workspace array\nIt is VERY IMPORTANT to compute this argument from the real_workspace_size output produced by tox_loess_required_workspace .\nThe minimum valid value is 100000_int32 . Read more… real(kind=real64), intent(out) :: tmp_hat_diag (n) Diagonal elements of the hat matrix real(kind=real64), intent(out) :: fitted_values (n) Fitted (smoothed) values of y at the evaluation points integer(kind=int32), intent(out) :: ierr Error code public  subroutine loess_fit_robust_impl (n, x, y, weights, eval_points, span, degree, max_neighborhood_size, compute_influence, save_factorization, n_iters, tmp_int_workspace, int_workspace_size, tmp_real_workspace, real_workspace_size, tmp_hat_diag, tmp_robust_weights, tmp_combined_weights, tmp_residuals, tmp_permutation_indices, fitted_values, ierr) Author Vivian Bass License MIT Perform robust LOESS fitting with bisquare reweighting Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer(kind=int32), intent(in) :: n Total number of data points real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: x (n) Predictor variable array real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: y (n) Response variable array real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: weights (n) Weight array for data points real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: eval_points (n,1) Evaluation points (x values at which the fitted curve is computed) real(kind=real64), intent(in) :: span Smoothing parameter for LOESS\nThe minimum valid value is EPS_LOESS .\nThe maximum valid value is 1.0_real64 . integer(kind=int32), intent(in) :: degree Degree of the LOESS polynomial\nThe minimum valid value is 0_int32 .\nThe maximum valid value is 2_int32 . integer(kind=int32), intent(in) :: max_neighborhood_size Maximum neighborhood size logical(kind=c_bool), intent(in), optional :: compute_influence Influence calculation flag\nThe default value is .false. . logical(kind=c_bool), intent(in), optional :: save_factorization Save matrix factorization flag\nThe default value is .false. . integer(kind=int32), intent(in), optional :: n_iters Number of robust iterations\nThe minimum valid value is 1_int32 .\nThe default value is 3_int32 . integer(kind=int32), intent(out) :: tmp_int_workspace (int_workspace_size) Integer workspace array integer(kind=int32), intent(in) :: int_workspace_size Required size of the integer workspace array\nIt is VERY IMPORTANT to compute this argument from the int_workspace_size output produced by tox_loess_required_workspace .\nThe minimum valid value is 10000_int32 . Read more… real(kind=real64), intent(out) :: tmp_real_workspace (real_workspace_size) Real workspace array integer(kind=int32), intent(in) :: real_workspace_size Required size of the real workspace array\nIt is VERY IMPORTANT to compute this argument from the real_workspace_size output produced by tox_loess_required_workspace .\nThe minimum valid value is 100000_int32 . Read more… real(kind=real64), intent(out) :: tmp_hat_diag (n) Diagonal elements of the hat matrix real(kind=real64), intent(out) :: tmp_robust_weights (n) Robust bisquare weights (updated each iteration, initialized to 1.0) real(kind=real64), intent(out) :: tmp_combined_weights (n) Combined weights: product of user weights and robust weights (weights(i) * robust_weights(i)) real(kind=real64), intent(out) :: tmp_residuals (n) Residuals (y - fitted_values), used to compute bisquare robust weights integer(kind=int32), intent(out) :: tmp_permutation_indices (n) Permutation indices array (from NetLib bisquare weight computation) real(kind=real64), intent(out) :: fitted_values (n) Fitted (smoothed) values of y at the evaluation points integer(kind=int32), intent(out) :: ierr Error code","tags":"","url":"module/tox_loess_impl.html"},{"title":"tox_errors – TensorOmics","text":"error handling module for tensor-omics It keeps its tox_ name because it defines Tensor Omics' error vocabulary, but it lives in src/f42/ because f42 itself depends on it: it sits below f42 in the stack, not above. Uses f42_safeguard ieee_arithmetic iso_fortran_env iso_c_binding Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial integer(kind=int32), public, parameter :: ERR_OK = 0 no error, operation successful integer(kind=int32), public, parameter :: ERR_FILE_OPEN = 101 could not open file integer(kind=int32), public, parameter :: ERR_READ_MAGIC = 102 could not read magic number integer(kind=int32), public, parameter :: ERR_READ_TYPE = 103 could not read array type error integer(kind=int32), public, parameter :: ERR_READ_NDIMS = 104 could not read number of dimensions integer(kind=int32), public, parameter :: ERR_READ_DIMS = 105 could not read array dimensions integer(kind=int32), public, parameter :: ERR_READ_CHARLEN = 106 could not read character length integer(kind=int32), public, parameter :: ERR_READ_DATA = 107 could not read array data integer(kind=int32), public, parameter :: ERR_WRITE_MAGIC = 112 could not write magic number integer(kind=int32), public, parameter :: ERR_WRITE_TYPE = 113 could not write array type error integer(kind=int32), public, parameter :: ERR_WRITE_NDIMS = 114 could not write number of dimensions integer(kind=int32), public, parameter :: ERR_WRITE_DIMS = 115 could not write array dimensions integer(kind=int32), public, parameter :: ERR_WRITE_CHARLEN = 116 could not write character length integer(kind=int32), public, parameter :: ERR_WRITE_DATA = 117 could not write array data integer(kind=int32), public, parameter :: ERR_FILE_ADD = 121 